    <bpmn:process id="W_W54A" name="W54A. BIR Computerized Accounting System (CAS) Registration" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New entity incorporation, new ERP system deployment, major system upgrade requiring re-registration, or annual permit renewal
Frequency: Initial registration per entity (5 entities); annual renewal per BIR requirements; re-registration if system undergoes major changes
Volume: 5 entity registrations initially; 5 annual renewals thereafter
Owner: Regulatory Officer
Participants: Regulatory Officer, CIO, Controller, CFO, external ERP vendor, BIR Regional Office
Source: workflow W54A — BIR Computerized Accounting System (CAS) Registration</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W54A_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W54A_Lane1" name="Regulatory Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W54A_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W54A_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W54A_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W54A_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W54A_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W54A_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W54A_Lane2" name="IT Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W54A_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W54A_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W54A_Lane3" name="Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W54A_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W54A_Lane4" name="BIR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W54A_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W54A_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W54A_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W54A_Start6" name="New entity incorporation, new ERP system deployment, major system upgrade requiring…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W54A_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W54A_Task7" name="Regulatory Officer obtains BIR CAS registration forms: BIR Form 1907…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Regulatory Officer obtains BIR CAS registration forms: BIR Form 1907 (Application for Authority to Print Receipts/Invoices, filed alongside the CAS application), together with system documentation package
Responsible (R): Regulatory Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 4 hours/entity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W54A_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W54A_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W54A_Task8" name="IT and ERP vendor prepare system documentation package per BIR requirements…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: IT and ERP vendor prepare system documentation package per BIR requirements: (a) system overview and architecture diagram, (b) data flow diagram showing transaction processing from source to GL, (c) security and access control documentation, (d) sample outputs: BIR-registered receipt format, sales invoice, purchase invoice, journal voucher, official receipt, books of accounts (general journal, general ledger, cash receipts/disbursements journals, sales/purchases journals), (e) data retention and backup procedures, (f) audit trail documentation, (g) BIR permit application letter signed by entity&#x27;s authorized representative
Responsible (R): IT Team / ERP Vendor
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–3 weeks/entity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W54A_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W54A_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W54A_Task9" name="Controller reviews and validates sample outputs for accounting accuracy: GL…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Controller reviews and validates sample outputs for accounting accuracy: GL account mapping, journal entry formatting, books of accounts layout compliance with BIR-prescribed format
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours/entity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W54A_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W54A_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W54A_Task10" name="Regulatory Officer submits CAS registration application to BIR Regional Office…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Regulatory Officer submits CAS registration application to BIR Regional Office (or Revenue District Office) where the entity is registered; pays registration fee per BIR schedule
Responsible (R): Regulatory Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1 day/entity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W54A_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W54A_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W54A_Task11" name="BIR evaluates application; may conduct system demonstration or on-site…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: BIR evaluates application; may conduct system demonstration or on-site inspection at BuildRight office; IT and Finance present system capabilities to BIR evaluators
Responsible (R): BIR / IT / Finance
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 days/entity (if inspection required)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W54A_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W54A_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W54A_Task12" name="BIR issues CAS Permit (Authority to Use Computerized Accounting System) per…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: BIR issues CAS Permit (Authority to Use Computerized Accounting System) per entity; permit includes registered system name, entity TIN, permit number, and conditions of use
Responsible (R): BIR
Accountable (A): —
Duration: External (2–6 months from submission)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W54A_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W54A_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W54A_Task13" name="Regulatory Officer records CAS permit in system: permit number, issue date…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Regulatory Officer records CAS permit in system: permit number, issue date, expiry date (if applicable — some permits are perpetual unless system changes), entity TIN, authorized system name; uploads permit document to entity master
Responsible (R): Regulatory Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 15 min/entity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W54A_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W54A_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W54A_Task14" name="IT configures ERP to print BIR-registered receipt/invoice numbers per CAS…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: IT configures ERP to print BIR-registered receipt/invoice numbers per CAS permit: system generates sequential, non-skippable invoice/receipt numbers per BIR requirements; TIN, registered business name, and CAS permit number printed on all receipts per BIR format
Responsible (R): IT Team
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–3 days/entity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W54A_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W54A_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W54A_Task15" name="Annual renewal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Annual renewal (if required per BIR ruling): Regulatory Officer submits renewal documentation before expiry; confirms no material system changes since last registration
Responsible (R): Regulatory Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2 hours/entity/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W54A_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W54A_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W54A_Task16" name="Re-registration triggers">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Re-registration triggers: if ERP system undergoes major version upgrade, change of ERP platform, or change of entity legal name, Regulatory Officer files amended CAS registration with updated system documentation
Responsible (R): Regulatory Officer / IT
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Per initial process</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W54A_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W54A_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W54A_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W54A_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W54A_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: (none recorded)
Owner: Regulatory Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W54A_Assoc19" sourceRef="W54A_Annotation18" targetRef="W54A_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
