    <bpmn:process id="W_W477" name="W477. DENR Permit to Operate (PTO) &amp; Wastewater Discharge Permit (WDP) Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Installation of a new standby generator/STP, or upcoming permit expiry (tracked in Compliance Calendar)
Frequency: Renewed every 1 to 5 years (depending on generator capacity and discharge volume)
Volume: ~~205 locations (stores, DCs) with standby generators and STPs/septic systems
Owner: Pollution Control Officer (PCO)
Participants: Store Manager, DC Manager, DENR-EMB Inspectors, Accredited Stack Testing Firm, Third-Party Water Lab
Source: workflow W477 — DENR Permit to Operate (PTO) &amp; Wastewater Discharge Permit (WDP) Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W477_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W477_Lane1" name="Pollution Control Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W477_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W477_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W477_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W477_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W477_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W477_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W477_Lane2" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W477_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W477_Lane3" name="EMB Inspectors">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W477_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W477_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W477_Start5" name="Installation of a new standby generator/STP, or upcoming permit expiry (tracked in…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W477_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W477_Task6" name="Testing Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Testing Coordination: 90 days before permit expiry, PCO schedules mandatory environmental testing: (a) accredited laboratory draws effluent samples from the STP/septic system for biochemical analysis (BOD, COD, TSS), (b) accredited stack testing firm performs source emission testing (particulate matter, NOx, SOx) on standby generator exhausts.
Responsible (R): Pollution Control Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W477_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W477_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W477_Task7" name="Lab Results Analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Lab Results Analysis: PCO receives lab/stack test reports: (a) If compliant: moves to application; (b) If non-compliant: raises urgent EAM repair tickets (W47/W240) to service the STP (bacterial dosing, filter replacement) or tune the generator, then schedules re-testing.
Responsible (R): Pollution Control Officer
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W477_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W477_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W477_Task8" name="Documentary Package Compilation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Documentary Package Compilation: PCO compiles renewal documents: (a) Prior year PTO and WDP copies, (b) Water and air test certificates, (c) Water billing records (to calculate discharge fees), (d) Generator technical specifications, (e) PCO Accreditation Certificate.
Responsible (R): Pollution Control Officer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W477_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W477_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W477_Task9" name="Online Application Submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Online Application Submission: PCO uploads documents and files renewal application in the DENR-EMB OPMS portal; generates payment voucher for regulatory fees.
Responsible (R): Pollution Control Officer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W477_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W477_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W477_Task10" name="Fee Settlement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Fee Settlement: Finance processes the payment voucher (W7); PCO uploads the proof of payment to the EMB portal.
Responsible (R): Finance / PCO
Accountable (A): PCO
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W477_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W477_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W477_Task11" name="EMB Inspection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: EMB Inspection: Regional DENR-EMB inspectors conduct on-site audits of the store/DC: verify the generator&#x27;s exhaust stack height complies with the 5-meter rule, inspect the STP aeration tanks, and review onsite chemical storage.
Responsible (R): EMB Inspectors / PCO
Accountable (A): Store/DC Manager
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W477_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W477_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W477_Task12" name="Permit Issuance &amp; System Update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Permit Issuance &amp; System Update: Upon approval, EMB issues the digital PTO and WDP. PCO uploads the permits to the ERP Document Registry (W255), updates the Compliance Calendar, and updates the permit databases used for SMR/CMR reporting (W433).
Responsible (R): Pollution Control Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W477_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W477_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W477_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W477_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W477_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-307 (ensure controlled execution — Regulatory Permits &amp; Licenses (PA-22.1).) | - operational: Pollution Control Officer (PCO) review and approval gate
Owner: Pollution Control Officer (PCO)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W477_Assoc15" sourceRef="W477_Annotation14" targetRef="W477_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W477_Flow16" sourceRef="W477_Start5" targetRef="W477_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W477_Flow17" sourceRef="W477_Task6" targetRef="W477_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W477_Flow18" sourceRef="W477_Task7" targetRef="W477_Task8" />
