    <bpmn:process id="W_W479" name="W479. FDA License to Operate (LTO) for Household Hazardous Substances Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual license renewal cycle, or introduction of new regulated paints, thinners, varnishes, or solvent-based adhesives
Frequency: Renewed every 1 to 3 years depending on license validity period selected
Volume: Store-wide compliance across 200 retail stores selling chemical-based DIY goods, plus 4 DCs
Owner: Regulatory Compliance Manager
Participants: Qualified Person (technical representative), Category Managers, Store Managers, DC Managers, FDA Inspectors
Source: workflow W479 — FDA License to Operate (LTO) for Household Hazardous Substances Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W479_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W479_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W479_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W479_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W479_Lane2" name="Regulatory Compliance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W479_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W479_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W479_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W479_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W479_Lane4" name="Qualified Person">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W479_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W479_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W479_Lane5" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W479_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W479_Lane6" name="FDA Inspectors">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W479_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W479_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W479_Start8" name="Annual license renewal cycle, or introduction of new regulated paints, thinners…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W479_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W479_Task9" name="SKU Compliance Screening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: SKU Compliance Screening: Category Managers flag chemical, paint, and adhesive items in the SKU registry. Regulatory Compliance Manager cross-references each vendor&#x27;s Certificate of Product Registration (CPR) against the FDA database to ensure all stock is legally registered.
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Regulatory Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): Regulatory Compliance Manager
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W479_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W479_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W479_Task10" name="Technical Representative Assignment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Technical Representative Assignment: Regulatory Compliance Manager maintains the registered credentials of the designated &quot;Qualified Person&quot; (e.g. licensed pharmacist or chemist) required by the FDA to oversee chemical safety reporting.
Responsible (R): Regulatory Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W479_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W479_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W479_Task11" name="Site Inspection Audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Site Inspection Audit: Store and DC Managers inspect paint-mixing machines (W168) and hazardous chemical storage areas (W236) to verify compliance with FDA Good Distribution and Storage Practices (GDSP) guidelines (ventilation, warning signs, spill kits).
Responsible (R): Store Manager / DC Manager
Accountable (A): Regulatory Compliance Manager
Duration: 2 hours/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W479_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W479_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W479_Task12" name="Documentation Package Compilation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Documentation Package Compilation: Qualified Person compiles application requirements: (a) Business permit, (b) Lease contract, (c) Location and floor plans showing hazmat storage layout, (d) Notarized Qualified Person affidavit, (e) List of products to be distributed.
Responsible (R): Qualified Person
Accountable (A): Regulatory Compliance Manager
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W479_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W479_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W479_Task13" name="FDA Portal Submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: FDA Portal Submission: Qualified Person uploads documents and submits the LTO renewal/initial application on the FDA ePortal; generates the electronic payment voucher.
Responsible (R): Qualified Person
Accountable (A): Regulatory Compliance Manager
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W479_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W479_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W479_Task14" name="Application Fee Settlement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Application Fee Settlement: Finance processes the FDA payment voucher (W7). Qualified Person uploads the official receipt to the portal to activate the application evaluation queue.
Responsible (R): Finance / Qualified Person
Accountable (A): Qualified Person
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W479_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W479_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W479_Task15" name="On-Site FDA Audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: On-Site FDA Audit: FDA inspectors conduct physical or virtual inspection of stores/DCs to verify proper storage segregation, emergency procedures, and technical documentation.
Responsible (R): FDA Inspectors / Store Manager
Accountable (A): DC Manager (for DCs) / Store Manager (for stores)
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W479_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W479_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W479_Task16" name="LTO Issuance &amp; ERP Release">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: LTO Issuance &amp; ERP Release: FDA issues the digital LTO. Regulatory Compliance Manager uploads the permit to the Document Registry (W255), updates the Compliance Calendar, and updates the SKU master regulatory flag, authorizing procurement (W2) and sales.
Responsible (R): Regulatory Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W479_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W479_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W479_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W479_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W479_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-307 (ensure controlled execution — Regulatory Permits &amp; Licenses (PA-22.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Regulatory Compliance Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W479_Assoc19" sourceRef="W479_Annotation18" targetRef="W479_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
