    <bpmn:process id="W_W480" name="W480. CAAP Height Clearance Permit Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Construction of a new store/DC, major renovation, or installation of tall outdoor signage structures (pylon signs, cellular/radio antennas) near aerodromes
Frequency: Per construction project, or upon modification of tall structures in airport buffer zones
Volume: Relates to store/DC development projects located within 15 kilometers of airports
Owner: Engineering &amp; Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Participants: Project Manager, Store Design Architect, CAAP Aeronautical Engineers, Geodetic Engineer, LGU Building Official
Source: workflow W480 — CAAP Height Clearance Permit Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W480_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W480_Lane1" name="Store Design Architect">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W480_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W480_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W480_Lane2" name="Geodetic Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W480_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W480_Lane3" name="Project Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W480_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W480_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W480_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W480_Lane4" name="CAAP Engineers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W480_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W480_Lane5" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W480_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W480_Lane6" name="CAAP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W480_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W480_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W480_Start8" name="Construction of a new store/DC, major renovation, or installation of tall outdoor signage…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W480_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W480_Task9" name="Flight Path Proximity Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Flight Path Proximity Check: During site feasibility (W116), Store Design Architect uses geographical coordinates (W310) to assess proximity to airport runways and determine if CAAP buffer zones apply.
Responsible (R): Store Design Architect
Accountable (A): Engineering &amp; Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W480_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W480_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W480_Task10" name="Geodetic &amp; Topographic Survey">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Geodetic &amp; Topographic Survey: If the site is within CAAP buffer zones, Project Manager hires a CAAP-deputized Geodetic Engineer to perform an elevation survey and prepare a certified Geodetic Report detailing elevation and height.
Responsible (R): Geodetic Engineer
Accountable (A): Project Manager
Duration: 3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W480_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W480_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W480_Task11" name="Documentary Package Compilation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Documentary Package Compilation: Project Manager compiles the HCP application: (a) Certified Geodetic Report, (b) Site plans, (c) Elevation drawings showing highest point of structure/pylon sign, (d) Certified coordinate list.
Responsible (R): Project Manager
Accountable (A): Engineering &amp; Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W480_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W480_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W480_Task12" name="CAAP Submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: CAAP Submission: Project Manager submits the application to the CAAP Aerodrome Development and Management Service (ADMS) at the CAAP Main Office or regional office.
Responsible (R): Project Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W480_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W480_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W480_Task13" name="Aeronautical Technical Study">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Aeronautical Technical Study: CAAP Aeronautical Engineers evaluate the proposed structure height against flight path models and airport radar lines of sight.
Responsible (R): CAAP Engineers
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–45 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W480_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W480_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W480_Task14" name="Fee Settlement &amp; Lighting Requirements">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Fee Settlement &amp; Lighting Requirements: Finance processes the CAAP study fees (W7). CAAP issues structural specifications (e.g. painting sign towers in aviation orange/white, installing warning lights (W173)).
Responsible (R): Finance / Project Manager
Accountable (A): Project Manager
Duration: 2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W480_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W480_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W480_Task15" name="HCP Certificate Issuance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: HCP Certificate Issuance: CAAP issues the final Height Clearance Permit specifying the maximum allowable height.
Responsible (R): CAAP
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W480_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W480_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W480_Task16" name="LGU Permit Release &amp; Archiving">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: LGU Permit Release &amp; Archiving: Project Manager submits the CAAP HCP to the LGU Building Official to secure the building permit (W54/W225); uploads the digital HCP copy to the Document Registry (W255).
Responsible (R): Project Manager
Accountable (A): Engineering &amp; Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W480_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W480_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W480_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W480_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W480_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-307 (ensure controlled execution — Regulatory Permits &amp; Licenses (PA-22.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Engineering &amp; Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W480_Assoc19" sourceRef="W480_Annotation18" targetRef="W480_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W480_Flow20" sourceRef="W480_Start8" targetRef="W480_Task9" />
