    <bpmn:process id="W_W1203" name="W1203. Philippine Data Privacy Act (RA 10173) Compliance Audit, DPO Reporting &amp; NPC Registration" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual compliance audit cycle; or triggered by new NPC circular, data breach incident, or new data processing activity
Frequency: Annual comprehensive audit; quarterly DPO report; continuous monitoring
Volume: Covers 600,000 loyalty customer records, 6,762 employee records, 5,200 trade account records, 200 corporate account records, ~42,900 ecommerce customer records/month
Owner: Data Protection Officer (DPO)
Participants: DPO, CIO, VP Legal, CHRO, Marketing Manager (Loyalty), Ecommerce Ops Manager, IT Security Manager
Source: workflow W1203 — Philippine Data Privacy Act (RA 10173) Compliance Audit, DPO Reporting &amp; NPC Registration</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1203_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1203_Lane1" name="DPO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1203_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1203_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1203_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1203_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1203_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1203_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1203_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1203_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1203_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1203_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1203_Start3" name="Annual compliance audit cycle; or triggered by new NPC circular, data breach incident, or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1203_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1203_Task4" name="Data processing inventory update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Data processing inventory update: DPO updates the company&#x27;s Data Processing System Inventory: (a) lists all systems processing personal data (POS, ecommerce, loyalty, HR/payroll, CRM, CCTV, job applicant database), (b) for each system: identifies data subjects, categories of personal data collected, purpose of processing, legal basis (consent, legitimate interest, contractual necessity, legal obligation), data retention period, and access controls, (c) registers any new data processing activities with NPC per NPC Circular 2016-02
Responsible (R): DPO
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1203_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1203_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1203_Task5" name="Privacy Impact Assessment (PIA)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Privacy Impact Assessment (PIA): For new or significantly changed data processing activities (e.g., new ecommerce feature, new CCTV system, new loyalty data sharing with partners): (a) DPO conducts PIA identifying privacy risks, (b) documents mitigation measures, (c) obtains sign-off from system owner and CIO, (d) files PIA with NPC if processing involves sensitive personal data or automated decision-making
Responsible (R): DPO
Accountable (A): CIO / VP Legal
Duration: 8–20 hours per new processing activity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1203_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1203_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1203_Task6" name="Consent management audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Consent management audit: DPO audits consent collection mechanisms: (a) loyalty program enrollment: verify consent form includes all required elements per NPC (purpose, data collected, retention, right to withdraw), (b) ecommerce registration: verify privacy notice is displayed and consent captured at registration, (c) job applicant data: verify consent in employment application, (d) CCTV signage: verify prominent signage at all 200 stores and 4 DCs notifying customers of CCTV recording; flags any consent mechanism that does not meet NPC standards
Responsible (R): DPO
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1203_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1203_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1203_Task7" name="Data subject rights response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Data subject rights response: When a data subject exercises rights under RA 10173 (access, correction, deletion, withdrawal of consent): (a) DPO receives and logs request within 24 hours, (b) verifies identity of requester, (c) coordinates with relevant system owner (IT for data extraction, HR for employee data, Marketing for loyalty data), (d) responds within 10 business days (NPC-mandated timeline), (e) executes requested action (provide copy, correct data, delete/de-identify, stop processing); tracks all requests in data privacy register
Responsible (R): DPO
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2 hours/request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1203_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1203_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1203_Task8" name="Data breach response protocol">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Data breach response protocol: In the event of a data breach (unauthorized access to personal data): (a) IT Security Manager notifies DPO within 1 hour of detection, (b) DPO assesses breach severity within 24 hours: (i) number of data subjects affected, (ii) sensitivity of data compromised, (iii) likelihood of harm, (c) if breach poses significant risk: DPO notifies NPC within 72 hours per NPC Circular 2016-03, (d) notifies affected data subjects &quot;in the most expeditious time possible,&quot; (e) implements containment and remediation measures, (f) documents full breach timeline and response for NPC investigation
Responsible (R): DPO / IT Security
Accountable (A): CIO / CEO
Duration: Variable (depends on severity)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1203_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1203_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1203_Task9" name="Annual NPC compliance report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual NPC compliance report: DPO prepares and submits annual compliance report to NPC: (a) summary of data processing activities, (b) number of data subject requests received and resolved, (c) number and nature of any data breaches, (d) PIAs conducted, (e) employee privacy training completion rate, (f) planned improvements for next year; registers/updates DPO appointment with NPC
Responsible (R): DPO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 8 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1203_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1203_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1203_Task10" name="Employee privacy training">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Employee privacy training: DPO conducts annual data privacy training for all employees: (a) online training module covering RA 10173 basics, BuildRight&#x27;s data privacy policy, handling of customer data at POS, and breach reporting procedure, (b) mandatory completion for all 6,762 employees, (c) tracked in LMS per W74 (learning and development), (d) refresher training for roles with high data access (cashiers, HR staff, customer service, IT)
Responsible (R): DPO / HR
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 4 hours/year (DPO) + 30 min/employee</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1203_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1203_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1203_Task11" name="Quarterly DPO board report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Quarterly DPO board report: DPO presents quarterly data privacy status to CEO and CIO: (a) compliance status and upcoming NPC requirements, (b) data subject request volume and resolution, (c) any breaches or incidents, (d) consent management audit findings, (e) recommendations for privacy program improvements
Responsible (R): DPO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1203_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1203_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1203_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1203_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1203_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-307 (ensure controlled execution — Regulatory Permits &amp; Licenses (PA-22.1).) | - operational: pre-drafted breach notification templates and designated breach response team; operational: centralized consent management platform integrated with all customer-facing systems; operational: annual mandatory training (Step 7) and simple POS-level procedures for customer data handling
Owner: Data Protection Officer (DPO)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
