    <bpmn:process id="W_W1244" name="W1244. Philippine LGU Business Permit Batch Renewal, Monitoring &amp; Compliance Tracking for Store Network" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual business permit renewal cycle (typically January); also triggered by new store opening per W16 or store relocation per W45
Frequency: Annual renewal for all 200 stores + 4 DCs + HQ; ~205 permits/year renewal + ~10–15 new permits for new stores
Volume: ~205 locations × multiple permits per location (mayor&#x27;s permit, barangay clearance, fire safety inspection certificate per W476, sanitary permit per W448, environmental clearance per W477) = ~800–1,000 permit transactions/year
Owner: Legal &amp; Compliance Officer
Participants: Legal &amp; Compliance Officer, Store Manager, DC Manager, Finance – Tax, VP Legal, LGU Processing Officer
Source: workflow W1244 — Philippine LGU Business Permit Batch Renewal, Monitoring &amp; Compliance Tracking for Store Network</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1244_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1244_Lane1" name="Legal &amp; Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1244_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1244_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1244_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1244_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1244_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1244_Lane2" name="Store Manager or Legal Rep">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1244_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1244_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1244_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1244_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1244_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1244_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1244_Start6" name="Annual business permit renewal cycle (typically January); also triggered by new store…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1244_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1244_Task7" name="Annual renewal calendar preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual renewal calendar preparation (November): Legal &amp; Compliance Officer compiles renewal calendar: (a) extract all location permit data from ERP (permit type, issuing LGU, expiry date, renewal deadline per LGU); (b) sort by deadline (earliest first); (c) identify new requirements for each LGU (some LGUs update requirements annually); (d) generate renewal task list with deadlines and assigned owners
Responsible (R): Legal &amp; Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 8–16 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1244_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1244_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1244_Task8" name="Pre-renewal compliance check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pre-renewal compliance check (December): For each location: (a) verify BIR registration current per W260; (b) verify fire safety inspection certificate obtained per W476; (c) verify sanitary permit current per W448 (if applicable); (d) verify barangay clearance current; (e) verify DENR clearance current per W477 (for DCs and stores with hazmat per W236); (f) verify no pending LGU violations or citations
Responsible (R): Legal &amp; Compliance Officer / Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min/location</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1244_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1244_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1244_Task9" name="Batch document preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Batch document preparation: Legal &amp; Compliance team prepares renewal documents in batches by LGU: (a) completed application form (per LGU format); (b) previous year&#x27;s permit (photocopy); (c) financial statements or gross receipts declaration for local business tax computation per W802; (d) BIR registration certificate; (e) lease contract or proof of location ownership; (f) fire safety inspection certificate; (g) barangay clearance; (h) authorized representative documents (if not Store Manager personally filing)
Responsible (R): Legal &amp; Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min/location</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1244_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1244_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1244_Task10" name="Filing &amp; payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Filing &amp; payment: (a) file application with LGU Business Permit and Licensing Office (BPLO); (b) pay local business tax per W802 (computed on gross receipts or fixed rate per LGU ordinance); (c) LGU processes application (timeline: 1–10 business days per ARTA, though actual varies widely by LGU); (d) some LGUs offer online filing via LGU portal — leverage where available
Responsible (R): Store Manager or Legal Rep
Accountable (A): Legal &amp; Compliance Officer
Duration: 1–3 hours/location</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1244_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1244_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1244_Task11" name="Permit receipt &amp; posting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Permit receipt &amp; posting: Upon receipt of renewed permit: (a) scan and upload to ERP document management per W255; (b) update permit master data with new expiry date per W54; (c) post physical permit at store entrance (mandatory display per Philippine law); (d) update compliance dashboard
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Legal &amp; Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 15 min/location</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1244_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1244_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1244_Task12" name="Compliance monitoring &amp; escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Compliance monitoring &amp; escalation: System monitors: (a) flag permits expiring within 30 days; (b) auto-notify Store Manager and Legal &amp; Compliance Officer; (c) if permit expired: escalate to VP Legal and COO; (d) if renewal delayed &gt;15 days past deadline: assess risk of LGU action and consider temporary operating procedures
Responsible (R): System / Legal &amp; Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1244_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1244_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1244_Task13" name="New store permit processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: New store permit processing: For ~10–15 new stores/year per W16: (a) initiate new business permit application during site selection per W116; (b) process concurrent with store construction per W225; (c) obtain permit before store opening date — store cannot open without valid business permit; (d) add to compliance monitoring calendar
Responsible (R): Legal &amp; Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: Per W16</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1244_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1244_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1244_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1244_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1244_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-307 (ensure controlled execution — Regulatory Permits &amp; Licenses (PA-22.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Legal &amp; Compliance Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1244_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1244_Annotation15" targetRef="W1244_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
