    <bpmn:process id="W_W1304" name="W1304. BIR Computerized Accounting System (CAS) Registration, Compliance &amp; Audit Readiness" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Initial ERP system registration with BIR; annual compliance review; or BIR CAS audit notification
Frequency: Initial registration (one-time per system change); annual compliance review; BIR audit per notice
Volume: 5 legal entities requiring CAS registration; 200 store locations with BIR-registered POS per entity
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance / Tax Accountant
Participants: Tax Accountant, VP Legal &amp; Compliance, CIO, POS System Administrator, External Tax Advisor, BIR Revenue District Officer (RDO)
Source: workflow W1304 — BIR Computerized Accounting System (CAS) Registration, Compliance &amp; Audit Readiness</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1304_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1304_Lane1" name="Tax Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1304_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1304_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1304_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1304_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1304_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1304_Lane2" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1304_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1304_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1304_Start4" name="Initial ERP system registration with BIR; annual compliance review; or BIR CAS audit…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1304_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1304_Task5" name="Initial CAS registration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Initial CAS registration: (a) Tax Accountant prepares CAS registration package per BIR RDO requirements: (i) BIR Form 1907 (Application for Registration of CAS), (ii) system description document: ERP modules, data flow diagram, hardware/software inventory, (iii) sample outputs: sales invoice, official receipt, purchase order, journal voucher, financial statements, (iv) sworn statement attesting that the system produces accurate and complete books of account, (v) system security and data integrity controls documentation; (b) Tax Accountant submits package to BIR RDO per entity registration location (BuildRight entities registered in Davao City RDO); (c) BIR may conduct site inspection or demo before approving registration; (d) upon approval: BIR issues Certificate of Registration for CAS — maintain on file at HQ and submit copies to each RDO where entity has business operations; (e) register each POS terminal (600 total across 200 stores) with BIR per store&#x27;s RDO — each terminal receives a unique BIR registration number displayed on all receipts
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 2–4 weeks initial setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1304_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1304_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1304_Task6" name="System change notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System change notification: (a) for any material change to the CAS: (i) ERP version upgrade, (ii) new module activation, (iii) POS system software update, (iv) change in hardware (server migration, cloud hosting change), (v) new integration (e.g., new e-wallet provider, new ecommerce feature) — Tax Accountant evaluates whether BIR notification or re-registration is required per Revenue Regulations; (b) for material changes: submit BIR Form 1905 (Application for Registration Information Update) with description of change; (c) BIR may require re-inspection for significant changes; (d) maintain change log documenting all CAS modifications with dates, descriptions, and BIR notification status
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant / CIO
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Per change event: 2–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1304_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1304_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1304_Task7" name="Annual CAS compliance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Annual CAS compliance review: Annual, Tax Accountant conducts compliance review: (a) verify all POS terminals are BIR-registered and displaying correct registration numbers on receipts; (b) verify all books of account registered with BIR match the ERP&#x27;s chart of accounts and reporting structure; (c) verify e-invoicing readiness: system can generate BIR-compliant electronic sales invoices with required fields (TIN, business name, address, VAT registration, item description, quantity, unit price, VAT amount, total); (d) verify data retention: electronic records for past 10 years are accessible and readable; (e) verify system access controls: user access logs, audit trail, and segregation of duties are documented; (f) review any BIR issuances (Revenue Regulations, Revenue Memorandum Orders) issued in the past year that may affect CAS requirements; (g) compile annual CAS compliance report for VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 1–2 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1304_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1304_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1304_Task8" name="BIR CAS audit response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: BIR CAS audit response: If BIR issues CAS audit notice: (a) VP Legal &amp; Compliance coordinates response: (i) designate audit liaison (Tax Accountant + IT representative), (ii) prepare documentation: system description, sample outputs, access controls, data retention, change log, POS registration records; (b) during BIR examination: (i) BIR examiners may request live demo of POS, invoice generation, financial report generation, (ii) BIR may verify that system-generated reports match submitted tax returns, (iii) BIR may check data integrity (sample journal entries traced to source documents); (c) post-examination: address any BIR findings within prescribed timeframe; (d) if BIR issues assessment: VP Legal evaluates assessment validity and recommends response (comply, protest, or appeal)
Responsible (R): VP Legal / Tax Accountant / CIO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Per audit event: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1304_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1304_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1304_Task9" name="E-invoicing readiness &amp; migration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: E-invoicing readiness &amp; migration: (a) monitor BIR e-invoicing mandates — BIR is phasing mandatory e-invoicing starting with large taxpayers (BuildRight qualifies); (b) Tax Accountant and CIO evaluate current system&#x27;s e-invoicing capability: (i) can the ERP generate BIR-compliant e-invoices (JSON/XML format per BIR specification)?, (ii) can the system transmit e-invoices to BIR&#x27;s portal in real-time or near-real-time?, (iii) what development/integration work is needed?; (c) develop e-invoicing implementation plan with IT and vendor; (d) test e-invoicing with BIR sandbox environment before go-live; (e) phased rollout: start with corporate/B2B invoicing, then expand to POS transactions
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant / CIO
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Per mandate timeline</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1304_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1304_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1304_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1304_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1304_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-307 (ensure controlled execution — Regulatory Permits &amp; Licenses (PA-22.1).) | - operational: modifications during the audit period
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance / Tax Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1304_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1304_Annotation11" targetRef="W1304_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
