    <bpmn:process id="W_W1421" name="W1421. Philippine LGU Business Permit Annual Renewal, Local Business Tax Filing &amp; Multi-Location Compliance Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual business permit renewal deadline (January 20 per LGU calendar); or quarterly local business tax filing; or new store opening requiring new permit per W54
Frequency: Annual renewal per location (200 stores + 4 DCs + HQ = 205 locations); quarterly local business tax filing per location
Volume: 205 locations × 1 annual renewal = 205 renewals/year (concentrated in January); 205 locations × 4 quarterly tax filings = 820 tax filings/year
Owner: Regulatory Compliance Officer
Participants: Regulatory Compliance Officer, VP Legal, Store Manager, DC Supervisor, Controller, LGU Liaison
Source: workflow W1421 — Philippine LGU Business Permit Annual Renewal, Local Business Tax Filing &amp; Multi-Location Compliance Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1421_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1421_Lane1" name="Regulatory Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1421_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1421_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1421_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1421_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1421_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1421_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1421_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1421_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1421_Start4" name="Annual business permit renewal deadline (January 20 per LGU calendar); or quarterly local…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1421_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1421_Task5" name="Annual renewal preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual renewal preparation (November–December): Regulatory Compliance Officer initiates renewal preparation: (a) system generates renewal checklist per location: current permit number, expiry date, LGU-specific requirements, (b) compile required documents per LGU: (i) current year financial statements (audited), (ii) BIR Certificate of Registration, (iii) SEC Certificate of Incorporation, (iv) Barangay Clearance, (v) CTO/CTC (Community Tax Certificate), (vi) fire safety inspection certificate per W1051, (vii) building occupancy permit, (viii) environmental compliance certificate (for DCs with hazmat storage per W1222), (c) Store Managers verify local requirements (LGU requirements change frequently — some LGUs add new requirements annually)
Responsible (R): Regulatory Compliance Officer / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 4–6 weeks (Nov–Dec)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1421_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1421_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1421_Task6" name="Renewal filing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Renewal filing (January): (a) Regulatory Compliance Officer submits renewal applications to 205 LGUs: (i) for Davao City locations (HQ + 8 stores + DC1 = 10 locations): filed in person at Davao City Hall Business Bureau, (ii) for other Mindanao/Visayas/Luzon locations: filed through LGU liaison or authorized representative, (iii) some LGUs accept online filing (increasingly available), (b) pay annual business permit fee per location: fee = fixed rate × floor area + gross revenue-based assessment (varies by LGU, typically PHP 15,000–50,000 per store per year), (c) obtain new permit sticker/certificate for posting in store
Responsible (R): Regulatory Compliance Officer / LGU Liaison
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2–3 weeks in January</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1421_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1421_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1421_Task7" name="Quarterly local business tax filing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quarterly local business tax filing: (a) system calculates quarterly local business tax per location: gross revenue for the quarter × LGU-specific tax rate (0.5–2.0%), (b) Regulatory Compliance Officer prepares tax declarations per LGU format, (c) Store Managers or LGU Liaison submits and pays at LGU treasury office, (d) payment receipts filed in compliance document repository
Responsible (R): System / Regulatory Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours/location/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1421_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1421_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1421_Task8" name="Compliance tracking and alerting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Compliance tracking and alerting: (a) system maintains LGU compliance calendar per location: permit expiry dates, quarterly tax due dates, inspection schedules, (b) automated alerts: 30-day, 14-day, and 7-day reminders before expiry/deadline, (c) Regulatory Compliance Officer reviews compliance dashboard weekly: identify approaching deadlines, overdue filings, penalty exposure, (d) Store Managers receive mobile app notification for their location&#x27;s upcoming deadlines
Responsible (R): System / Regulatory Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1–2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1421_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1421_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1421_Task9" name="Penalty management and dispute resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Penalty management and dispute resolution: (a) if a location misses a renewal or filing deadline: Regulatory Compliance Officer assesses penalty (typically 25% surcharge), (b) coordinate with LGU to negotiate penalty abatement where possible (Philippine LGUs have discretion to waive penalties for first-time late filers), (c) if LGU issues a closure notice: escalate to VP Legal for emergency resolution, (d) document all LGU interactions for audit trail
Responsible (R): Regulatory Compliance Officer / VP Legal
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: As needed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1421_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1421_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1421_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1421_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1421_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-307 (ensure controlled execution — Regulatory Permits &amp; Licenses (PA-22.1).) | - operational: early preparation starting November
Owner: Regulatory Compliance Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1421_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1421_Annotation11" targetRef="W1421_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1421_Flow13" sourceRef="W1421_Start4" targetRef="W1421_Task5" />
